# Growth Factor

`flex-grow` is a unitless number (default 0). If there's extra space, items grow proportionally to their `flex-grow` value.

```css
.item1 { flex-grow: 1; }
.item2 { flex-grow: 2; }
/* item2 gets twice the extra space */
```
If all items have `flex-grow: 1;`, they share space equally.

slides.codeSnippet:
.col {
  flex-grow: 1;
  flex-basis: 0; /* start from zero size */
}
/* Shorthand: flex: 1; */

